    <summary>Sovereign privacy browser (Firefox 150 fork) with a live network monitor and honeypot</summary>
    <description><![CDATA[
# BearBrowser

A sovereign, privacy-first browser — a LibreWolf-mirror fork of **Firefox 150** built
to be the most private browser you can run.

## Features

- **Hardened anti-fingerprinting** — Canvas, WebGL, AudioContext, fonts, timing,
  navigator and WebRTC surfaces, layered on Firefox's resistFingerprinting.
- **BearNet** — a built-in loopback network monitor. See every host this browser
  (or the whole machine) is talking to as a live graph + world map, with
  click-to-block and on-demand OSINT (RDAP / reverse-IP / certificate transparency).
  All geolocation is resolved from a **local** GeoIP database — no external lookups.
- **BearTrap honeypot** — detects and attributes fingerprinting scripts, and blocks
  canary-token exfiltration outright.
- **No telemetry, no Google services, no cloud dependency** — fully local-first.

## Install notes

This package installs the real BearBrowser Windows build from the project's GitHub
release. The build is currently **unsigned** (no code-signing cert yet), so Windows
SmartScreen may warn on first run.
    ]]></description>
    <releaseNotes>https://github.com/SourceOS-Linux/BearBrowser/releases/tag/v150.0.1</releaseNotes>
